by nicolas-grekas at 2026-08-02T08:06:32Z

Thanks Amoifr, the nullable case and the fixtures are right now. Rebased on 8.2 and made three changes before merging.

Added the `UPGRADE-8.2.md` entry under `Serializer`. Three shapes that returned raw data before now throw: an element matching no member of the union, a class the denormalizer does not know, and a key whose type does not match the declared one. That is the kind of change people need to read before upgrading.

Shortened the CHANGELOG entry to one line. It also named the wrong exception: for a union of classes with required constructor arguments the exception is `MissingConstructorArgumentsException`, which extends `RuntimeException` and not `NotNormalizableValueException`. That matches what the existing direct-union path does, so only the wording was wrong, and the detail belongs in the docs rather than in the changelog.

Added `testDenormalizeArrayOfUnknownClassUnionTypesRejectsElements`. Your comment said both tightenings were pinned by tests, but only the float case was; the unknown-class one had none. It fails on base for the right reason.

Note the rebase now conflicts with #63803, which merged in the meantime, so I resolved the CHANGELOG by keeping both entries.

The PR description was rewritten to read as documentation, and it ends with the points a symfony-docs PR should carry. The nested `array<array<Foo|Bar>>` and `iterable<Foo|Bar>` cases are stated there as out of scope.
